\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Buenaventura: Ctrl Bk Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2001\par 03:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 29/06/01 01-59G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0159GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  - - 29/06/01 01-59G \par \par \uc2  0159GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 29/06/01 02-01G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0201GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MANILA (Dow Jones)--Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael\par Buenaventura said the bank hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support a weaker peso so\par far in Friday's session, but is willing to come into the market if\par necessary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso came under renewed pressure in early trading from regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses and domestic security tensions, with the dollar hitting\par a high so far in the session of PHP52.470, up from PHP52.370 at the\par previous close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Several dealers said they believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars around\par PHP52.380 to support the peso, and prevent the dollar from breaching the\par key level of PHP52.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked to confirm this, Buenaventura told Dow Jones Newswires: "No, we\par are not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but we might come in if necessary."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Buenaventura said he believe resistance for the dollar at PHP52.50\par would hold through Friday's session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the peso is under pressure from weak regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par quarter-end corporate demand for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I suspect there'll be resistance (at PHP52.50) and maybe exporters\par will come in (to sell dollars)," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market has been abuzz with talk over the past days that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been discreetly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most of this week has seen the dollar firmly entrenched over the key\par level of PHP52, its highest level since the leadership crisis that raged\par in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ditas Lopez and Alastair McIndoe, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 632-885-0288; alastair.mcindoe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6t02xi3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
