\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen losses hurt, politics grip rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2001\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were caught in the yen's downdraft late on Monday, which provided players with an excuse to add to their long dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro strengthened at the expense of the yen after talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept investors on alert in a market thinned by holidays in London and New York. \par \par \uc2  Political concerns also added to the region's woes. Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid warned in a nationally televised speech that any attempts to oust him would break Southeast Asia's most populous country apart. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, the interest rate tussle between the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged on. A local newspaper reported that the government was preparing to order the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to force up deposit rates by 1.5 percentage points to spur spending. \par \par \uc2  But Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra denied the report, saying he had never ordered the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do so. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah wilted past 11,500, briefly hitting one-month lows of 11,720, as Indonesia's leadership crisis dragged on. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to President Wahid's comments, which stopped short of carrying out his threat to declare a state of emergency. \par \par \uc2  Wahid is scrambling to save his presidency as parliament is set to meet on Wednesday to decide whether to press ahead with a special impeachment session of the top legislative body. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said the rupiah escaped further losses because local corporates had little appetite for dollars around these levels and state banks were also spotted selling dollars around 11,650. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht settled in a well-worn 45.56-45.62 range, caught between buying by government-linked exporters and selling from offshore banks, Bangkok dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The continuing battle between the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over interest rates weighed on sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said the government would decide on the best level for interest rates after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports on its policy review on June 4. \par \par \uc2  Deposit rates currently stand at around two to three percent, with lending rates at seven to eight percent. Thai banks are unwilling to lend given their mountain of non-performing loans. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar struggled in the wake of poor economic data, hitting 32-month lows of 34.50 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let up its usual dogged defence in late trade. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold up to $1.5 billion to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, beginning its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session around 33.495. But it later let the local dollar go in the face of heavy demand for dollars and the disappointing economic data. \par \par \uc2  After the close, the bank said it would enter the market to "maintain order" if necessary, attributing the local dollar's sharp fall to "untrue rumours". \par \par \uc2  While it had been bracing for bad news, the market was still glum over first quarter gross domestic product data issued after the close on Friday. The economy grew by a mere 1.06 percent on year, against forecasts of 3.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  The top economic planning agency said earlier in the day the economy slowed in April with no recovery in sight. Its index of leading indicators in April slipped 0.5 percent on month to 93.3. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the Taiwan dollar could see some relief as the market is heavily long of dollars. Charts showed dollar/Taiwan looking hugely overbought, with a 14-day relative strength index reading of 98. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso dipped against Friday's 50.50 close, though it was off its day's low of 50.96. Local corporates seeking to repay foreign debt bought the dollar on dips towards 50.60. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said it was also weighed by ongoing political uncertainty coupled with weekend news of gunmen believed to be Muslim rebels seizing 20 people in a tourist resort in the southern Philippines. \par \par \uc2  The market was also eyeing a special Congressional session to debate a key power reform bill, viewed as a litmus test of the government's commitment to reform. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar was in limbo, stuck in a tight 1.8080-1.8118 range over the course of the day, but dealers said the mood was hurt by growing tension in Indonesia and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  Local banks and U.S. names were offering the dollar at around 1.8110, stirring jitters about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which admitted it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market earlier this month to support the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  "At any rate, people want to buy the dollar with all sorts of reasons from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Indonesia to Taiwan, but they can't because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Given such fears, dealers expected the Sing dollar was unlikely to weaken beyond 1.8180 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won closed near the top end of its Monday trading range of 1,293.2-1,298.0 despite the yen's retreat, buoyed by exporter dollar offers and some fund inflows. \par \par \uc2  But the upside was capped amid caution ahead of major economic data this week, including April industrial output on Tuesday and the May consumer price index on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast industrial output fell 0.6 percent last month from March because of dwindling exports and sluggish domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  Inflation is expected to be tame due to seasonal factors. \par \par \uc2  "We expect negative month-on-month headline inflation for the first time this year. Declines in fruit and heating oil prices are likely to be the main course," Salomon Smith Barney said. \par \par \uc2  "Quite stable CPI figures should be favourable to the bond market. But headline inflation tends to be modest in May because of the seasonal stabilization in agricultural food prices," the bank said in a report. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0835 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.05\tab  120.58\tab    -0.39\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8110\tab  1.8063\tab    -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.500\tab  33.495\tab    -2.91\par  Korean won   1293.80\tab 1288.90\tab    -0.38\par  Baht\tab      45.58\tab   45.51\tab    -0.15\par  Peso\tab      50.72\tab   50.51\tab    -0.42\par  Rupiah\tab 11580.00     11440.00\tab    -1.21\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move