\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mixed but jittery on oil price, stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 03:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned \par \par \uc2  mixed after an easier start amid continued worries over rising \par \par \uc2  oil prices and on fears of capital outflows from local stock \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      "Given the moves in the equity markets overnight and the \par \par \uc2  oil prices pushing up higher, we are likely to see weakeness \par \par \uc2  across the boards today," said Rebecca Patterson, regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2      Patterson said the downside for some of the regionals could \par \par \uc2  be limited but only on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities. \par \par \uc2      On Monday largely ignored encouraging data released by some \par \par \uc2  of the countries. \par \par \uc2      "What we are seeing today is very sentiment driven market \par \par \uc2  and if there are what the market perceives as negative events \par \par \uc2  tend to get more magnified and events that could be taken as \par \par \uc2  positive are ignored," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  The euro struggled to keep afloat a touch above its \par \par \uc2  Monday's life low, but dealers see high chance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  testing another trough below $0.8500 in near term. \par \par \uc2  The yen was hovered close to 107 to the dollar after \par \par \uc2  Dallas Fed President McTeer's said he sees little risk of U.S. \par \par \uc2  "hard landing," but added risks to U.S. economy still tilted \par \par \uc2  toward higher inflation. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso wobbled close to the key psychological support of \par \par \uc2  46 to the dollar and dealers said only fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could keep players from testing \par \par \uc2  that level. \par \par \uc2  "There is already talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in the \par \par \uc2  market but no one is sure. Given the levels such confusion is \par \par \uc2  not surprising," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said worries about a fresh military campaign \par \par \uc2  launched by Manila against Muslim rebels in the south of the \par \par \uc2  country and a deteriorating fiscal balance would also keep the \par \par \uc2  peso under pressure. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The momentum of outflows from Taipei stock is likely to \par \par \uc2  keep the local dollar under pressure, but trading was likely to \par \par \uc2  be cautious after Monday's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rising oil prices and the weakness of the \par \par \uc2  equity market has not only hurt sentiment but has raised \par \par \uc2  concern about the outlook of the economy. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign funds are leading the selling in the stock market \par \par \uc2  which suggests that foreign investors are getting a bit \par \par \uc2  sceptical about the country's economic outlook or probably the \par \par \uc2  political scene," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday foreign investors were net sellers of T$1.807 \par \par \uc2  billion in domestic equities, extending Saturday's net selling \par \par \uc2  of T$53 million. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht retained its bearish tone due to persistent dollar \par \par \uc2  bids from both offshore and onshore parties amid talk a few \par \par \uc2  large funds were covering short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Several dealers in Singapore said they did not expect to \par \par \uc2  see any strong dollar pullback until the U.S. unit reached \par \par \uc2  42.50 which was the next target. \par \par \uc2  But some argued that recent high baht funding cost in the \par \par \uc2  offshore market should substantially slow down a pace of the \par \par \uc2  decline. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/baht offshore forwards were quoted around \par \par \uc2  +15.5/+20.5 satang/dollar compared with +17.0/+22.0 early on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar/baht gets to 42.50, I expect to see a flurry \par \par \uc2  of profit taking there. We favour selling the dollar at that \par \par \uc2  level for 42.20," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar retreated alongside the regionals and the \par \par \uc2  battered euro which is believed to account for a sizeable chunk \par \par \uc2  in its trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Singapore's positive export data released on Monday was \par \par \uc2  clouded by bearish sentiment prevailing in the region. \par \par \uc2      Its non-oil domestic exports surged 27.3 percent \par \par \uc2  year-on-year on August, beating the most bullish estimate, on \par \par \uc2  the back of strong demand in electronic products from the U.S. \par \par \uc2  and Europe. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to move in a narrow \par \par \uc2  range of 1.7450-1.7485 this week as players started to be \par \par \uc2  cautious about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of America said if the Sing dollar managed to break \par \par \uc2  through 1.7485, the next target would be 1.7500 in the \par \par \uc2  near-term. KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won regained its composure after falling sharply \par \par \uc2  alongside local stocks on Monday, with local dealers expecting \par \par \uc2  the unit to move between 1,127-1,135 during the day. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the current weakness was driven mostly by a \par \par \uc2  collasped deal between Ford and Daewoo Motor. \par \par \uc2      "But the market will move on. The government will be forced \par \par \uc2  to do something about this. Moreover, South Korea still has \par \par \uc2  very strong external balances which should be supportive to the \par \par \uc2  won," said a dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Dollar profit taking helped lift the rupiah above the 8,700 \par \par \uc2  mark, but not the market gloom. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has now returned to the neutral zone on the \par \par \uc2  14-day relative strength index, indicating there could be room \par \par \uc2  for further downside for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Salomon Smith Barney suggested that once the rupiah \par \par \uc2  retreated to 8,550, players should start building long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions again. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0121 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.00\tab  106.91\tab    -0.08\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7450\tab  1.7466\tab    +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    31.257\tab  31.255\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1129.50\tab 1130.00\tab    +0.04\par  Baht\tab      42.20\tab   42.20\tab    +0.00\par  Peso\tab      45.85\tab   45.82\tab    -0.07\par  Rupiah\tab  8620.00\tab 8670.00\tab    +0.58\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 C