\par\par \b \uc2  Philippine Stocks - Factors to Watch - Sept 7. \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 03:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MANILA, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Following are some of the main factors likely to affect Philippine stocks on Thursday: \par \par \uc2  Renewed weakness in the peso and the slump in the Nasdaq overnight will likely spur selling in Philippine shares. \par \par \uc2  OUTLOOK \par \par \uc2  * "Definitely the weakness in the peso will have a negative effect on the market, as well as the dramatic fall in the Nasdaq. These will combine to support some profit-taking in the market," said Andrew Long, research head of Vickers Ballas Securities \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  Inc. \par \par \uc2  * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to prevent the peso sliding towards its historic low of 46.50 to the dollar but the bank decided against a hike in overnight rates to protect the peso. \par \par \uc2  * The main index is seen testing its 1,500 psychological support if the peso continues to fall further towards the 46 to the dollar level, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  * The Nasdaq composite index slumped 3.13 percent on Wednesday after losing over two percent in the previous session as pessimistic comments on technology companies spooked the market. \par \par \uc2  MARKET CLOSINGS ON WEDNESDAY \par \par \uc2  * The Philippine main index lost 14.96 points to 1,527.80 points. \par \par \uc2  * The peso closed slightly firmer at 45.50 to the dollar from 45.595. \par \par \uc2  * PLDT's American Depositary Receipts slid $0 1/16 to end at $17. \par \par \uc2  * The Dow climbed 50.03 points to 11,310.64 points. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS TO WATCH \par \par \uc2  * Oil refiner Petron Corp has secured a $120 million three-year loan facility from a syndicate of banks, the proceeds of which will be used to refinance an existing loan. \par \par \uc2  * EBC Investments Inc is selling 10 percent of its stake in Equitable PCIBank to a foreign regional partner, Inquirer newspaper reported quoting a top bank official. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9708rhg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
