\par\par \b \uc2  Philippine peso wobbly on corporate demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2000\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MANILA, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso fell again on Thursday as month-end corporate dollar buying added to lingering concerns over the drawn-out crisis with Moslem rebels in the south. \par \par \uc2  After opening stronger at 45.075, the peso reversed direction and slid to 45.137 to the dollar at the close, against 45.087 at Wednesday's finish. \par \par \uc2  "Since it's month-end, a lot of corporate demand came out. There's a lot of buying from certain sectors because it's imports season," a trader from a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Banks also sold the peso owing to jitters over the potentially depressing effect on investment and the economy of all the media attention being showered on foreign tourists kidnapped by Moslem rebels in the southern \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , another trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso from breaching the 45.15 to the dollar level, which they said could prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide all the way to the previous year-low of 45.20. \par \par \uc2  And for the second day in a row, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura denied the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars to support the beleagured peso. \par \par \uc2  "We were not there," Buenaventura told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Yet traders continued to assert it had. \par \par \uc2  "He would deny it but we think he was (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) at 45.14," a trader from a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The volume of trades through the Philippine Dealing System totalled a moderate $93.5 million, down from $137.8 milion on Wednesday when banks also pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso is expected to trade in the 45.10 to 45.20 range against the dollar on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8v09iuh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
