\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2 ' Buenaventura: No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  On Spot  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2000\par 08:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- Despite renewed losses in the peso Tuesday, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's a waste of time and money," governor Rafael Buenaventura told reporters, reiterating the authority's policy of only selling dollars on the spot market in the event of heavy speculative pressures against the peso. \par \par \uc2  In afternoon trading Tuesday, the dollar averaged PHP43.567 on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP43.530 at the previous close. The greenback hit a day-high of PHP43.60, setting a fresh 21-month high against the peso. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after the outbreak of Asia's 1997 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost a costly battle defending the peso from speculative attack. Since then, it has generally allowed the peso-dollar rate to be determined by the market. \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura attributed the peso's decline Tuesday to weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  However, traders say the peso is also weak on a raft of economic and political concerns, including low local interest rates, a slowing economy and national security worries. \par \par \uc2  To be sure, the narrowing differential between U.S. and Philippine interest rates has prompted a significant shift towards dollar-denominated investments. Although U.S interest rates were kept unchanged last month, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively lowered its overnight borrowing rate from a flat rate of 10% to a three-tiered system that offers a lower rate for funds in excess of PHP5 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Amethyst Ma, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-892-5590; amethyst.ma@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw74037wj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
