\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Limp in cautious trade, baht sags. \b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2000\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 15 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  remained soft in late Monday trade, though volumes thinned \par \par \uc2  ahead of a key decision on U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2      Players stayed on the sidelines before a Federal Reserve \par \par \uc2  meeting on Tuesday, widely expected to result in a 50 basis \par \par \uc2  point rate hike. \par \par \uc2      Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were relatively steady as markets focused \par \par \uc2  on the Fed meeting as well as talk of European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  interevention to help the euro. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   held near Friday's two-week highs against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Against the yen, it\tab      was holding just shy of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's four-week peaks just above 100.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was trading near 109 yen\tab   with cooled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enthusiasm for Japanese equities. The Nikkei average\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell 0.25 percent on Monday, stuck near six-month lows hit last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht slipped through its key 39.20 per dollar support,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par partly because of the rupiah fallout.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the baht was being sold as a proxy due to poor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity in the rupiah. Chartists said it could test 39.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par soon now that 39.20 was broken.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Clouded by the region's bearish tone, the baht barely drew\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support from positive news on the non-performing loans and debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par restructuring front.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Thailand said on Monday that total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-performing loans carried by the Thai financial sector fell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 37.02 percent of total loans in March from 38.09 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won shed early gains on late dollar short-covering and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong dollar buying in the non-deliverable forward (NDF)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Seoul said weakness in the yen and other Asian\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted won selling in overseas forward markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the government's purchase of $100 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to pay off its foreign debt also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helped to offset the won's gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won is expected to trade between 1,113 and 1,116 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, staying hostage to moves in overseas forward markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The chief of Korea's Financial Supervisory Commission said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in late trade the economy could face trouble unless corporate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and financial restructuring is completed by the end of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was still weighed, testing seven-month lows at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,750 per dollar as pessimism over Indonesia's economic and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political prospects persisted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia reported first quarter gross domestic product\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth of 3.21 percent year-on-year, below market expectations\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 4.2 to 6.5 percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia also said GDP growth in the second quarter was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to be less than one percent compared to the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Abdurrahman Wahid said he had never promised he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would act to boost the rupiah if it did not rebound by Monday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par denying comments made last Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wahid had said the government had a plan to prop up the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it did not rebound by Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Support was seen pegged at Friday's low of 8,750 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, while resistance was at 8,345.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso dipped against the dollar in sympathy with other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura told reporters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the debt market, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' benchmark 91-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Treasury-bill rate fell at the weekly auction on Monday despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations of higher local rates due to a looming rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. rates on May 16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rate, used by banks to price loans, dropped to an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average of 8.69 percent against last week's 8.746 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar drifted lower alongside its regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par counterparts and the yen, but wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept it supported the right side of 1.73 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eddy Kong, chartist at MMS Standard & Poors put near-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support for the Sing at 1.7310-20, with resistance at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7240-45.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is focused on Singapore's first quarter economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par report due later in the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Undoubtedly, the first quarter growth would be strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (around 7.0 year-on-year) on the back of strong manufacturing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par output," SEB Merchant Banking said in a report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But with a recent survey showing businesses are less\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par optimistic about the economic outlook, investors would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking out for the composite leading index for further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confirmation," the report said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was easier as losses in domestic stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and withdrawals of foreign capital in local equities dampened\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prop up the unit, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was light.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0957 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.33\tab  108.23\tab    -1.01\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7292\tab  1.7243\tab    -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr    30.767\tab  30.735\tab    -0.10\par  Korean won   1114.60\tab 1114.20\tab    -0.04\par  Baht\tab      39.25\tab   38.87\tab    -0.97\par  Peso\tab      41.50\tab   41.45\tab    -0.12\par  Rupiah\tab  8540.00\tab 8330.00\tab    -2.46\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.33\tab  102.21\tab    -6.51\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7292\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.77\par  Taiwan dlr    30.767\tab  31.380\tab    +1.99\par  Korean won   1114.60\tab 1135.00\tab    +1.83\par  Baht\tab      39.25\tab   37.45\tab    -4.59\par  Peso\tab      41.50\tab   40.20\tab    -3.13\par  Rupiah\tab  8540.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -18.33\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\pa