\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Domestic factors rule, baht slides. \b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2000\par 04:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  directionless in early trade on Wednesday, guided mostly by \par \par \uc2  domestic and technical factors with Tokyo closed for the Golden \par \par \uc2  Week holiday. \par \par \uc2      The baht dipped further on sales from large investment \par \par \uc2  houses and broad-based dollar short covering triggered by its \par \par \uc2  fall below 38.25 on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The dollar is expected to retain its bullish tone against \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen\tab     and the euro\tab     in the near-term as strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. new home sales in March reaffirmed the outlook for higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tuesday's news of President Wahid pledging no more cabinet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reshuffles failed to provide a boost to the rupiah and it still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traded on the weaker side of the 8,000 level early Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said dollar/rupiah remained firm above 8,000, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the recent highs of 8,075 in sight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Political uncertainty following the sacking of two of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wahid's economic ministers last Thursday sent the rupiah to six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month lows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won was a little firmer against the dollar in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early trade on Wednesday as players looked to unwind dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions, wary of possible inflows from foreign investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying local stocks, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Players are watchful of possible dollar inflows from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign equity investment in recent sessions," said a foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers forecast the won would move between 1,109 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,110.6 on the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Finance Ministry reiterated its warning on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the won's rapid rise against the dollar was not desirable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given Korea's dwindling trade surplus and the dollar/yen moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar fell on a steady slope in early trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday, though its pace has somewhat eased as it inched\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closer to the psychologically important level of 1.7200 where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers were nervous about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the MAS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the overall strength of the US dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helping to push down the Singapore unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the market saw 1.7200 as pivotal, because the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar had not closed above that level since March 8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some retreat was expected on profit-taking though support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was seen at 1.7100, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso barely drew support from robust export data and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par talk of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' exports in March rose 10.6 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the same period last year to $2.988 billion. The January-March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports were up 9.6 percent year-on-year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to allow the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso to drop below 41.30 where stop-loss orders and active\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedging activity are likely to emerge.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht came off against the dollar on heavy sales from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major investment houses, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit was also pressured by dollar short-covering and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss orders as the dollar/baht looked set to test\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance of 38.50 where exporter offers are lined up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chart suggested the baht could head toward 38.65 if the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 38.50 level is broken. Some houses suggested clients reassess\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the trend only when the baht pulls back to 37.90.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar moved in a narrow range with a downward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias as investors were cautious about China ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par official inauguration of President Chen Shui-bian's government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers expected the unit to be underpinned by comments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Moody's Investors Service that its outlook for Taiwan Aa3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign and local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings remains stable despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent political uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moody's said that in its opinion, the ratings outlook for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan will be most immediately determined by economic, rather\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than by political developments.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0138 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.61\tab  108.54\tab    -0.06\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7182\tab  1.7162\tab    -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    30.720\tab  30.669\tab    -0.17\par  Korean won   1109.60\tab 1109.90\tab    +0.03\par  Baht\tab      38.43\tab   38.29\tab    -0.36\par  Peso\tab      41.27\tab   41.27\tab    +0.01\par  Rupiah\tab  8022.00\tab 8015.00\tab    -0.09\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.61\tab  102.21\tab    -5.89\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7182\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.15\par  Taiwan dlr    30.720\tab  31.380\tab    +2.15\par  Korean won   1109.60\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.29\par  Baht\tab      38.43\tab   37.45\tab    -2.55\par  Peso\tab      41.27\tab   40.20\tab    -2.58\par  Rupiah\tab  8022.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -13.05\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 