\par\par \b \uc2  Philippine Peso Ends Higher On Dollar Inflows \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 12:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- The Philippine peso closed Thursday higher against the dollar, buoyed by dollar liquidity as some foreign and offshore banks unwound long-dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 41.12 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, down from Wednesday's PHP41.13. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  averaged PHP41.129, lower than PHP41.172 in the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Volume rose to $163 million from $150.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Traders don't see any fundamental reason behind the peso's latest strength, given the weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the lingering political concerns over the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading many to suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's up (peso) because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader for a foreign bank, echoing a widely-held suspicion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is injecting dollars in the market to defend the peso after it hit a six-month low of PHP41.20 early this week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied it's selling dollars through some foreign banks to prop up the sagging peso. "No, we were not in the market," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the selling pressure the dollar is encountering at or close to the PHP41.20 level has forced some of those with long-dollar positions, particularly offshore banks, to unwind their positions. \par \par \uc2  "It appears the peso won't be allowed to breach the PHP41.20 for the moment, so some offshore banks are reducing their long positions," said trader with another foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  -By Cris Larano; 632-892-5590; cris.larano@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1060 1853 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4601s7d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
