\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Buenaventura Says CB Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2000\par 03:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said Wednesday that the peso-dollar rate continues to be market-oriented and the authority isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Let the market believe what it wants to believe," Buenaventura told Dow Jones Newswires, commenting on market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has supplied dollars to the market to relieve pressure on the peso. \par \par \uc2  In morning trading Wednesday, the dollar averaged 41.179 pesos on the spot market, up from PHP41.150 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Tight dollar liquidity and strong demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from domestic corporations and offshore funds, coupled with concerns over the political situation in the Philippines, have kept the dollar above PHP41 for the past few trading days. \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura said he expects the peso-dollar rate to be "fairly stable" Wednesday and said the peso market isn't out of kilter with the trend of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In morning trading Wednesday, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed, but the Thai baht, which is closely tracked on the peso market, was weaker against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura said that at a certain level, which he didn't name, dollar-selling will likely kick in on the peso market and help strengthen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura noted with approval March's "good" inflation rate was lower than expected. \par \par \uc2  As reported, inflation in March rose 3.3% on year, far lower than many economists' forecasts of around 3.8%. \par \par \uc2  "The good news is that the inflation rate is rather below the range and with the peso stable vis-a-vis regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , perhaps there is no need to raise overnight rates, but I'm not ruling it out," he said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, Buenaventura said March's inflation data will determine whether it's necessary to raise policy rates at Friday's meeting of the Monetary Board. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main tool to control domestic liquidity, is at 8.75%. \par \par \uc2  -By Amethyst Ma and Alastair McIndoe 632 8792 5590 alastair.mcindoe@dowjones,com \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010802dw4500aw4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
