\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht respite, zloty sub-parity. \b0\par\par\uc2 921 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1999\par 12:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 29 (Reuters) - The Thai baht drew breath on Wednesday amid confusing signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while equally mixed pointers from the National Bank of Poland left the zloty below its basket parity. \par \par \uc2  The buoyant Czech crown tested fresh resistance levels against the euro, but South Africa's rand eased slightly after this week's sharp rise on the back of surging world gold prices. \par \par \uc2  Kenya's shilling fell sharply on fears that government attempts to woo the International Monetary Fund were not going well. \par \par \uc2  Emerging Asia was mixed as the dollar hovered just below 107 yen, with the Philippine peso continuing south on expectations of further baht weakness. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found some respite, firming slightly but staying on the weak side of 41 to the dollar after assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Cherdthawee Chareonpitak said it should not drop below 40, based on economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Speaking in Singapore, Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi chimed in with the same message that fundamentals justified a stronger baht. \par \par \uc2  Only a day earlier, Thailand's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Tanya Sirivedhin, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw a range of 41-42 baht per dollar as "acceptable". \par \par \uc2  "The problem with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that they're trying to manipulate a level, and that's always problematic," said Gerry Celaya, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  technical analyst at American Express Bank in London. "We still think it's going to go towards 42." \par \par \uc2  The peso opened at an 11-month low of 41.20 to the dollar, although it retraced some ground after President Joseph Estrada said he was not ruling out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more concerned at the speed of the peso's slide than its actual level against the dollar, as a soft \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would support exports. \par \par \uc2  "We don't think (Estrada) has any great affection for a mega-strong \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Celaya said. "It's really the pace of things and the fact that people are actually talking about it that's upset them." \par \par \uc2  MIXED SIGNALS IN POLAND \par \par \uc2  The zloty, which slipped to around 0.12 percent below its basket parity on Tuesday, eased further on Wednesday to settle around 0.29 percent below the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts blamed the slide on political uncertainty after news that the junior partner in the coalition government could ask for the dismissal of Prime Minister Jerzy Buzek. \par \par \uc2  But others said it was drifting ahead of Friday's balance of payments data for August, and was still taking its cue from Tuesday's comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz that the zloty would hover around the centre of its trading band in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Recent signs from Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been mixed, with another member of its Monetary Policy Council saying last week he saw the zloty ending the year at 3.0-4.0 percent above parity, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown mild volatility as a result. \par \par \uc2  "Politics in Poland really hasn't appeared to enter into market equations this year," said Juliet Sampson, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "Major cabinet shakeups are unlikely and there will be an impact (on the zloty) only if it looks like the coalition will break up." \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown was challenging strong resistance at 35.60 to the euro and analysts saw it firming further. \par \par \uc2  "The bias has to be on strengthening, given FDI (foreign direct investment) flows, the strong current account and trade picture and the fact that we've seen no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Sampson said. \par \par \uc2  The Kenyan shilling lurched beyond 77 to the dollar amid fears that the government was making poor headway in trying to persuade the IMF to resume lending to the cash-strapped East African country. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Chris Okemo is leading a mission to Washington in a bid to convince the IMF to start negotiations on a resumption of lending, which was cut off in mid-1997 in protest at official corruption. \par \par \uc2  ((Gill Tudor, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6414, fax 583 7239, gill.tudor@reuters.com)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     35.60   35.67   -0.19%   2.29%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.34    4.31    0.61%   6.63%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 256.54  256.34    0.08%   2.13%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 43.28   43.24    0.08%   0.65%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 16,455  16,445    0.06%  50.27%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   4.45    4.48   -0.67%  13.23%\par South Africa\tab \tab    5.97    5.96    0.25%   2.13%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    77.10   76.20    1.18%  25.16%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.27