\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Jolted by domestic woes, dlr demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,013 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1999\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0830 GMT - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended their losses \par \par \uc2  in late trade, ignoring the yen's resilience amid growing \par \par \uc2  confidence Japan would not win wider backing in its efforts to \par \par \uc2  rein in the rising yen. \par \par \uc2      Trade was thinned by a Japanese holiday but the dollar \par \par \uc2  slipped as far as 103.44 yen as remarks by U.S. officials \par \par \uc2  dampened fears the G7 would come up with a plan for joint \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this weekend's meeting. \par \par \uc2      New York Fed President William McDonough said current \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen levels are not a concern for the U.S. economy, while \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said the dollar would \par \par \uc2  do "fine" as long as U.S. fundamentals remained healthy. \par \par \uc2      Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  charted their own -- mostly southbound -- \par \par \uc2  course amid a raft of comments by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  officials, with Thailand and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  assuring the \par \par \uc2  market they did not plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht slid through a series of supports, \par \par \uc2  falling through the key 41.00 per dollar level in late trade on \par \par \uc2  persistent dollar demand from companies needing to make foreign \par \par \uc2  loan payments. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was monitoring the baht, but it \par \par \uc2  had not seen any sign of a speculative attack and had no plans \par \par \uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      It attributed the baht's recent decline to low domestic \par \par \uc2  interest rates and limited dollar supplies as exporters \par \par \uc2  withheld dollars due to low premiums in the swap market. \par \par \uc2      The market has also turned slightly more bearish about \par \par \uc2  Thailand in the wake of weaker than expected second quarter \par \par \uc2  growth. \par \par \uc2      The IMF said Thailand should grow 4.0 percent this year and \par \par \uc2  next but sounded warnings over the banking sector. \par \par \uc2      Banking reform was proceeding in the right manner but was \par \par \uc2  taking longer than expected, the IMF's director for Thailand \par \par \uc2  Ranjit Teja said. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso took its cue from the weak baht, sliding to \par \par \uc2  40.59, its lowest level in 10 months. \par \par \uc2      The peso has mirrored the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves of late as \par \par \uc2  the two countries compete in export markets. \par \par \uc2      Dollar demand from corporates and institutional investors \par \par \uc2  cutting their exposure to economies which are seen as holding \par \par \uc2  higher Y2K risks have also contributed to the peso's decline. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was not about to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the peso's fall was in line with general weakness \par \par \uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2      July production numbers for manufacturing fell year on \par \par \uc2  year. The government said the value of the production index \par \par \uc2  dipped 0.7 percent from July 1998, while its volume fell 4.6 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2      Net sales for July rose 3.1 percent year-on-year mainly due \par \par \uc2  to price hikes in petroleum products. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah slid to the wrong side of 8,600 per dollar \par \par \uc2  as thousands of students clashed with security forces in \par \par \uc2  Jakarta and Surabaya, protesting against a new security law \par \par \uc2  they argue gives the military even more power. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's parliament passed a watered down version of the \par \par \uc2  original draft on Thursday as police fired tear gas and warning \par \par \uc2  shots over the heads of students protesting in central Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  There was trouble in East Timor too, with Indonesian troops \par \par \uc2  accusing U.N. forces of firing warning shots at them, a charge \par \par \uc2  denied by the commander of the British contingent of the \par \par \uc2  multinational force in the territory. \par \par \uc2      Brigadier David Richards said Indonesian troops had fired \par \par \uc2  shots near his soldiers on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expected a rupiah rate of 6,850 to \par \par \uc2  7,600 to the dollar by end-1999, while year-on-year inflation \par \par \uc2  was seen falling to between three and five percent. \par \par \uc2      It said it was sticking to its 1999 GDP forecast of minus \par \par \uc2  two to zero percent and end-year one-month SBI interest rate of \par \par \uc2  10 to 12 percent. \par \par \uc2      The IMF said overnight it expected the Indonesian economy \par \par \uc2  to contract by 0.8 percent this year - much less than the 4.0 \par \par \uc2  percent decline it expected half a year ago - and to grow 2.6 \par \par \uc2  percent in 2000. \par \par \uc2  *** The Taiwan dollar was barely changed, with dealers \par \par \uc2  confident the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would maintain investor confidence \par \par \uc2  after Tuesday's huge earthquake, which has killed 2,100 people. \par \par \uc2      Liquidity was given an added boost after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  injected T$600 million worth of funds into the banking system. \par \par \uc2      The government said August industrial production rose 9.03 \par \par \uc2  percent year-on-year but September output was likely to be \par \par \uc2  affected by the quake. \par \par \uc2      August export orders rose 9.73 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Reuters had forecast on average a 7.98 \par \par \uc2  percent rise. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan has lowered its 1999 GDP forecast to 5.5 percent in \par \par \uc2  1999, compared with previous estimates of 5.74 percent. \par \par \uc2      *** South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is closed until Monday for a \par \par \uc2  national holiday which runs from September 23 to 25. \par \par \uc2      Seoul dealers saw the won firming after the holiday, given \par \par \uc2  expected demand for dollars from corporates and banks. \par \par \uc2      Demand would be triggered by principal and interest \par \par \uc2  payments of mid-term foreign loans in early October. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day THU 23 0837GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8700.00......8370.00.........-3.79% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........41.10........40.40.........-1.70% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.57........40.30.........-0.67% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7156.......1.7055.........-0.59% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.755.......31.755..........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1207.00......1207.00..........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....103.74.......104.47..........0.70% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par