\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Singson/Peso -2: Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Directly \b0\par\par\uc2 110 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1998\par 12:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA (Dow Jones)--Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Gabriel Singson said late Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to allow market forces to determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to remain out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and will only indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when there are wild fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main tool in helping the peso stabilize is raising its overnight borrowing rate, Singson said, noting it has long refrained from selling dollars on the Philippine Dealing System, the country's electronic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1154GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duas00jv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
