\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2 /Singson -2: Minimal  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1997\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Singson said the peso's steady appreciation has been achieved with minimal \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Singson noted that interest rates are also starting to soften, with the yield on the benchmark 91-day Treasury bill declining to 15.928% at this week's government securities auction from 16.341% at the previous auction. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, he said, interbank rates have dropped sharply, with the weighted average interbank call loan rate Tuesday at 13.1% compared to 42.5% on Nov. 6. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's priority is to see more exchange rate stability, which would pave the way for interest rates to fall further, Singson said. \par \par \uc2  He noted that various factors are at work in strengthening the peso, including significant remittance inflows from overseas Filipino workers and the bulk of local commercial demand for dollar having already been met. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, Singson said, 'apparently banks are also responding to the call for less aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, which could be counter-productive to banks' overall interests in the long run.' \par \par \uc2  Singson also noted that the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation has become calmer. \par \par \uc2  -By Alastair McIndoe: 00632 892-5590. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1000GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbb08k8b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal258