\par\par \b \uc2  Philippines De Ocampo-2:Sees Stabilization At Basement Level \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1997\par 18:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In Manila, Philippine stocks plunged to a record low Thursday, swept by a region-wide selloff following another downgrade for Asian shares by a U.S. investment bank. \par \par \uc2  The 30-share Philippine Stock Exchange Index lost 96.06 points, or 5%, closing at 1,832.91, its lowest level since the country's two stock markets were unified in 1994. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the massive sell-off across the region had been 'washed out' by Thursday's events, de Ocampo said 'it's not very easy to tell.' He said the sell-off was being encouraged by the 'continuing perception' of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability in the region, the need for Thailand to put into effect its economic reform program and the strength of the U.S. economy, which siphons off investment capital. \par \par \uc2  'So I think that it's likely to be stabilizing once it begins to appear that the prices of the stocks here have reached bargain basement levels,' he said. \par \par \uc2  De Ocampo said the Philippine decision to float the peso had proved a success. \par \par \uc2  'It has depreciated a little bit less in spite of the fact that there has been minimal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we have been able to preserve our reserves,' he said. \par \par \uc2  De Ocampo said that in the long run, significant changes needed to be made, chief among them 'greater information transparency' and 'better monitoring systems.' \par \par \uc2  He said the Philippines was trying to improve its own performance in those areas 'to make sure the market is fast becoming a better-informed market to have much better decisions rather than to go into a regime of regulations to stifle the market.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1613GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtan080oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
