\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2 /Singson -2: Cites Regional Trend,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 1997\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA (AP-Dow Jones)--Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Gabriel Singson said Friday he expects the peso to appreciate further against the dollar in coming days. \par \par \uc2  'There are strong indications that the peso will continue to strengthen in the days ahead,' Singson said before a meeting of the country's finance executives. \par \par \uc2  He cited as reasons for his optimism the strengthening of Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in recent days after more than three months of weakness, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to resume its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Philippine Dealing System, and the domestic measures taken to curb speculative plays on the peso. \par \par \uc2  The peso has rallied against the dollar in the past two trading days, buoyed mainly by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a new guideline preventing banks with excess dollars from borrowing pesos from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recently re-opened overnight lending window. \par \par \uc2  At Friday's close, the dollar averaged 33.156 pesos on the PDS, down 1.7 pesos from Thursday's average of 34.852 pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0836GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtaa07q4h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
