\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Regionals firm on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  fea. \b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 7 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained their footing on Tuesday as traders turned cautious about buying the dollar too aggressively amid growing talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in very thin markets. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, which stepped in to sell dollars when the rupiah slumped to an all-time low of 3,850 per dollar on Monday, was believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars in small amounts, pushing the rupiah to a high of 3,475 against its opening 3,600/50. \par \par \uc2  But persistent dollar demand from underhedged domestic companies and offshore funds jumping on the bandwagon pushed the rupiah back down to 3,640/50 by 0455 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's overnight gains after State Secretary Murdiono said the government would take steps to stabilise the rupiah, while remaining committed to free \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows, also helped sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stepped in to prop up the peso as it fell prey to pent-up dollar demand from foreign banks, diving to a record low of 35.981 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales from the 35.85 peso level helped turn the tide, pushing the peso back up to 34.65/75 by 0455 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The reimposition of a volatility band added to the market mayhem as the peso twice breached its limits before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading to trade suspensions. \par \par \uc2  The Bankers Association of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which operates the electronic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing system, decided late on Monday to reintroduce the band due to the peso's recent volatility. \par \par \uc2  It calls for a 30-minute recess if the peso moves outside a two percent limit. Upon resumption of trading, the band is narrowed to one percent and trading can be suspended two more times before being stopped for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Malaysian ringgit recovered sharply amid rumours in Singapore that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara Malaysia was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the unit. \par \par \uc2  But Malaysian dealers said they had not detected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence and most attributed the ringgit's rise to commercial demand and buying of the unit against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. names were said to be buying about $200-$300 million in ringgit/Sing," said one Singapore dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also plagued by fears Malaysia might implement a two-tier market, similar to Thailand's system, after Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's repeated calls for further curbs on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  There was confusion on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the format on a Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotation page was mistakenly changed early on Tuesday. The changes gave the impression a two-tier market had been created in the ringgit, rupiah and peso. \par \par \uc2  This mistake was subsequently corrected to reflect global consolidated contributions. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar recovered from its lows around 1.5470 to the U.S. dollar in line with the ringgit's move, but its gains were capped by buying of the ringgit/Sing cross. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was awaiting discussion in parliament, later in the day, about the impact of the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis on Singapore's economy and whether steps were being taken to address it. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht showed a firm bias on growing optimism about the government's finance sector reform package, due to be announced on October 15. \par \par \uc2  "It is a very narrow bid and offer, I think people are looking into the future for October 15 and some people think the news will come out positively," a local bank dealer in Bangkok said. Onshore baht was at 36.60/65 to the dollar while the offshore rate was at 35.65/75. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anchalee Koetsawang in Bangkok (662) 652-0642, Yoo Choon-Sik in Seoul (822) 727 5646, Lilian Kurunungan in Manila (632-841-8938) and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta701kzi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
