\par\par \b \uc2  IMF/Philippines -3: First Time Post-Mexico Procedure Used \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1997\par 23:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  To protect official reserves after an aborted attempt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a speculative attack on the peso, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved on July 11 to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The IMF noted that authorities moved to extend the existing credit facility to allow passage of key tax reforms and ultimately 'to support their action to float the peso in order to discourage speculative capital flows.' \par \par \uc2  The IMF decision was taken under an emergency assistance mechanism created in September 1995 after a controversial $17 billion standby credit was approved to help combat the December 1994 Mexican peso crisis. It was the first time the procedures were instituted, according to the fund. \par \par \uc2  The IMF called the Philippines performance under the existing credit arrangement 'satisfactory.' But it also noted that while its 'macroeconomic program remained broadly on track in the first quarter of 1997, the authorities faced a number of important challenges in the second quarter.' \par \par \uc2  It pointed to 'increasing turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, slippages in fiscal performance, and a delay in the passage of proposed tax reforms.' \par \par \uc2  The new cutoff date for the IMF credit arrangement is linked to the Philippine government's current schedule for legislative approval of the key tax measures, officials in Manila have said. \par \par \uc2  Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Gabriel Singson said earlier Friday in Manila as well that no decision has been made on the amount the Philippines would draw from the facility. But the funds would help replenish the country's foreign reserves, which have been depleted in the defense recently of the peso. \par \par \uc2  Singson disclosed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had received informal offers of credit of up to $2 billion from a number of U.S. and European banks. Even though terms weren't settled, he insisted the offers show 'the international community still believes in the good credit standing on the Philippines.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-07-97 \par \par \uc2  2124GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7i057gn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
