\par\par \b \uc2  Philippines should allow peso to fall - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Thatcher \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MANILA, July 10 (Reuter) - Pressure on the Philippine peso is reaching a stage when it may make more sense for the government to give in, end the pain, and let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slip a little, analysts and bankers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been adamant that the peso will not be allowed to fall against the dollar, but other government officials have been quoted this week as saying "devaluation" is being considered. The reports were quickly denied. \par \par \uc2  "When it walks like a duck and quacks like a duck, it must be a duck. Since high officials were the first to talk about it (devaluation) in a situation ripe for it, then the peso will have to depreciate soon," said Noel Reyes, analyst at Anscor Hagedorn Securities. \par \par \uc2  "(The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) can no longer rely on a few phone calls to bankers or a few innocuous, toothless warnings to the press against speculators to do the trick," he said. \par \par \uc2  If the speculative attack on the peso continues much longer, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to give in and stop defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  anyway, Reyes said. Other analysts agree. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have been depleted by repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and interest rates raised to levels which could hurt the economy. \par \par \uc2  Although the government has so far steadfastly declined to say how much money it has left in its kitty, official figures last put \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at just under $12 billion in May -- a bit more than three months' worth of imports. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $600 million in the market on Wednesday alone to defend the peso. \par \par \uc2  That would easily take care of the $500 million it raised last month by issuing a Yankee bond in the United States. \par \par \uc2  This has been the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' worst \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis in four years. Besides \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to raise its overnight interest rate to a high of 32 percent -- a 2-1/2 year high. \par \par \uc2  Many economists argue that the Philippine economy itself is in good shape and on target to become the next Asian tiger by the turn of the century. \par \par \uc2  Exports are booming, inflation is around record lows, the budget position of the government is in surplus and growth is likely to be at least six percent this year. \par \par \uc2  Even the grey peso market rate is virtually the same as the official rate. \par \par \uc2  So why should a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that has barely moved against the dollar in close to two years, suddenly have to fall? \par \par \uc2  Analysts say much of the speculation stems from fears -- especially among foreign investors -- that the Philippines cannot avoid being infected by the financial crisis in neighbouring Thailand. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Thai authorities allowed a de facto devaluation of the baht after prolonged speculative pressure. \par \par \uc2  "The underlying fundamentals are pretty good...It is what they are doing to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is worrying people," said Chris Hunt, head of research at W.I. Carr in Manila. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates have doubled in the past week simply to defend the peso and if they are prolonged they will inevitably cap growth. \par \par \uc2  "My feeling is that they (authorities) may be compelled to do something sooner rather than later," Hunt said. He added that a small drop in the peso's value would send the right message and not cause much of a shock. \par \par \uc2  "I think the peso will weaken. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't keep it up for very long," Luz Lorenzo, economist at Peregrine Securites said. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates now are punitive. The question is how much they will depreciate. But they'll do it gradually," she added. \par \par \uc2  She said that if the peso were to drop under the current pressure to around 28 to the dollar -- a depreciation of some six percent -- it would most likely bounce back fairly quickly afterwards because of general good economic conditons. \par \par \uc2  -- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8914 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7a02u19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
