\par\par \b \uc2  Southeast Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 /Baht -2: Baht Drops Sharply \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par 05:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were both sighted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also hiked short term rates to butress the peso by offering one-day reverse repurchase paper at 20% and, later in the morning, at 24%. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Thailand has also said it will maintain the capital controls imposed on offshore baht dealings in mid-May, limiting the ability of offshore players to take positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After the news of the float, the baht plunged by around 13% in the offshore spot market from around 24.70 baht/dollar in late trading Tuesday to around 28.50 baht/dollar early Wednesday, where it has since remained in very illiquid dealings. \par \par \uc2  Three-month forward rates in the dollar/baht have fallen to around 135 satang from around 225 satang late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The head of southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a regional bank said speculators who believe the baht move offers a good opportunity to bet against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are plotting a dangerous course, because the central banks in the region will protect each others' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'My 17 years on the markets here have taught me that you never muck around with Asian central banks - they always win, they always protect each other,' she said. \par \par \uc2  'I respect the fact that Thailand has severe economic problems,' she added, but the region's central banks, equipped with large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, will only allow devaluation on their terms. \par \par \uc2  In May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was among the regional central banks which joined in the Bank of Thailand's defence of the baht against a sustained speculative raid, exercising a number of bilateral cooperation agreements signed in the past two years. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank trader said that it look as if Bank Negara and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been quick to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early dealings Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  successfully to support the ringgit, and in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is not an open market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a better control on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than in Thailand,' he said. 'Although the Indonesian rupiah has fallen a little in the spot market, high interest rates will protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he added. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0349GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 4203 62553 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7204uyd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
