\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2 /Dlr Purchases -2: Easing  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1996\par 10:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA (AP-Dow Jones)--The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained a major player in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with net U.S. dollar purchases of $4.3 billion from Jan. 1 to Oct. 4. \par \par \uc2  But the latest data released Monday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  less actively at the Philippine Dealing System (PDS), where banks buy and sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for an average of 35% of volume from January through Oct. 4. By comparison, it accounted for 55% in January alone. \par \par \uc2  During the four days of October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $38 million, accounting for only 7.9% of the total $483.8 million dealt at the PDS. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a direct participant in the market only during the first two days. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-10-96 \par \par \uc2  0855GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013dsa7080xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
