\par\par \b \uc2  IMF/ \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Economy-4:Liquidity Rise Due To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1995\par 12:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The IMF mission will be visiting Manila for two weeks to see whether an upward revision in the Philippines monetary targets are warranted, even if inflation has been trending higher in the past three months. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, a National Economic Development Authority official said the government had just raised its 1995 inflation target to between 7.0% to 8.0% from the original 6.5%, citing inflationary pressures from an impending oil price hike. \par \par \uc2  The IMF has been concerned that higher liquidity would trigger inflation. \par \par \uc2  'They (IMF) see also the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we are buying,' Singson said. 'Whatever liquidity there is, is coming principally from these purchases in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These are externally generated rather than internally generated - it's not really money being released.' \par \par \uc2  Liquidity has also been pumped up by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to reduce the reserve requirement of commercial banks by two percentage points to 15% at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  As this move was meant primarily to ease the high interest rates in April, Singson noted that the rate of the bellwether 91-day treasury bill dropped to 13.36% last Friday from a high of 15.4% in mid-April. \par \par \uc2  'In the months ahead, Singson expects a stable interest rate regime with the continued resurgence in economic activity absorbing the observed growth in domestic liquidity,' another BSP statement said. \par \par \uc2  'Monetary policy will remain supportive of economic growth but will continue to be cuatious and vigilant of any inflationary pressures' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-95 \par \par \uc2  1001GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6q04sgr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
