\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -3:Want  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1995\par 06:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to attract people to lend at 25% so as to siphon off liquidity from the market. \par \par \uc2  Tightness in money supply is expected to push up interbank borrowing rates next week, which should put some pressure on the surging dollar. \par \par \uc2  Higher interest rates mean that it will be more expensive to carry dollars. It is also seen as inducing the unloading of some arbitrage dollars on the market in order to benefit from the higher yield. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the best way for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the dollar's rise is to start selling more dollars on the market now. \par \par \uc2  'We have sold everything we can, but we can not satisfy all the dollar requirements,' said a trader for a foreign bank. 'They have to add additional supply.' \par \par \uc2  Despite having unloaded as much as $70 million in previous sessions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been a big seller Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-02-95 \par \par \uc2  0518GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2o01b3n\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspa